  "about": "Which 3D model draws each building (docs/v2/model-kit.md). One table for the whole world: the fill's buildings, the engine's lots and shells, and named buildings. uses: for each building use, its models with the floors each can stand for ([least, most]); fill: any building of that use; named: preferred for a building the story names (detailed, heavier models). A building takes, of its use's models, those whose floors hold its own (else the nearest), then the ones whose proportions are nearest its own, one of them by a seed. A use with no model is drawn as a plain block. kinds: the use of a fill building with none of its own (a landscape's building kind). roles: the use of an engine lot or shell that has no building model (its role), and of a named building (what it was matched as). ancient: the models of an older world, by kind, '*' for any other; only buildings on ancient ground take them, and no modern use may name one. The library is apps/playground/src/data/architectureModels.json.",
